## PROBLEMS.md's two open questions — both resolved against the live checker

- **P4 (self-reference).** PROBLEMS.md warned the self-reference rule is a referent *scope* and might
  produce no error when set through MCP. It **does** error: the scope is enforced as a checker rule,
  reported as `out of search scope`. No fallback needed.
- **P7 (`servings = 0`).** PROBLEMS.md warned the `servings >= 1` validator might be silent when the
  value is set through MCP. It **does** error (`Property constraint violation`). No fallback needed.

## Three designed injections are silent and were replaced

Verified by injecting them, observing `errors=0`, and then reverting:

| designed | outcome | replacement |
|---|---|---|
| P6 — Cookbook with no recipes | **silent**: `Cookbook.recipes` is `0..n`, so an empty cookbook is legal (PROBLEMS.md anticipated this) | P6b — RecipeRef with an unset obligatory `recipe` reference |
| P10 — Ingredient with empty `name` | **silent**: a blank `INamedConcept.name` is not reported by any checker in this language | P10b — invalid `Unit` enum literal |
| P11 — Recipe with empty `name` | **silent**: same | P11b — non-integer `servings` |

The blank names were **restored** to `Salt` and `Toast` after the replacements landed, so every node
carries exactly one injected problem (PROBLEMS.md's "do not touch more than one thing per node").
That a blank name and an empty `0..n` collection produce no checker output is a finding in its own
right and is recorded in the round-6 report.

## Fixture naming note

The fixture table in `../../fixtures/README.md` says the `recipes` fixture is tarred **with the S1
sample Recipe and Cookbook roots deleted**. That rule exists for S3 only (its prompt demands
"exactly 40 Recipe roots plus the Cookbook"). S5 and S6 both need Recipe roots to exist, so round 6
introduced `recipes-full.tar.gz` — the same passing-S1 project with the samples **kept** — and built
`recipes-broken.tar.gz` on top of it. See the docs defect logged for the README.
